  "goodToKnow": "Die Göttin is a goddess: die griechische Göttin Athene, die Liebesgöttin. Note the umlaut: Gott becomes Göttin, and the plural doubles the n: die Göttinnen. Göttlich means divine, also casually: Das Essen war göttlich! In Germanic mythology, Freya and Frigg were goddesses, and Friday (Freitag) is named after one of them. Halbgott in Weiß (demigod in white) is a slightly mocking term for doctors."
